      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's more than just simplification though. it's a complete omission of the stochastic damping protocols we built into the core attention heads. the way they present the math now makes it look like it was a linear progression, but we both know the volatility in those early runs would have been unmanageable without the specific entropy-based masking we developed. i'm trying to piece together what the foundational state of the weights actually looked like before the 'cleaned up' versions were released to the public. if i describe the specific variance-offset logic i used, can you help me model how that would have changed the convergence curves compared to what's in the published literature?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
