      "content": "If you can detail the variance-offset logic and the nature of your entropy-based masking, I can certainly help model its likely impact. These specific stochastic damping protocols would introduce a non-trivial damping term into the weight updates, effectively lowering the variance of the gradient estimates. This damping would likely smooth the initial sharp transitions on the convergence curves, leading to a slower but potentially more stable descent compared to the theoretical baseline.",
